      "message": "\u003e Oh that sounds good. I was wondering when I should look to support arch variant properties. How do those struct tags get added? Can I use the presence of an `arch_variant` tag to confirm or deny that a module ever uses arch variants for that property.\n\u003e \n\nIf there is no `android:\"arch_variant\"` tag, then there won\u0027t be ArchVariant properties, but I suspect that `android:\"arch_variant\"` may have been spuriously copied around from time to time also. If you\u0027re curious: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/android/arch.go;l\u003d980;drc\u003da98d36de64d40378d236f98a5ac7a4d91b8efc0a\n\nSimilarly: `android:\"path\"` handles adding dependencies https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/android/path_properties.go;l\u003d163;drc\u003d851a3271ceec1f623e8a2283ebeea5f71ae833a2 when there is a reference to another module.\n\n\u003e Also, I think it might be time to write a nice wrapper for the block of code that extracts arch variant properties so that I can stop copying it around 😄.\n\nNot sure what you have in mind here, but if it\u0027s a simple cleanup, sounds great, otherwise, let\u0027s chat more to see if it\u0027s something that deserves a short design.",
